# jobs/dream.job
# ALLOWED_TOOLS is not set here — run-job reads it from ~/projects/trellis/skills/dream/
# SKILL.md's own frontmatter (single source of truth; see AGENTS.md). Until that skill lands,
# runs of this job fail closed rather than falling back to a stale copied list.
# SUCCESS is kb-commit, not exit0: the skill's last step always appends to the week's dream doc
# and commits it, even on an all-quiet night ("Nothing to consolidate." still gets a line) — only
# its sync step's rebase-conflict path skips it, and that path already ends the run non-zero on
# its own. exit0 alone would hide a run that exited 0 without actually doing the work.
DESCRIPTION="Nightly dream: consolidates memory and project docs from the day, prunes stale items, updates the week's dream doc, and messages running sessions about overnight changes."
SCHEDULE="*-*-* 06:00:00"
KIND="claude"
PROJECT="self-improve"
TIMEOUT_MIN=20
PROMPT="/dream"
SUCCESS="kb-commit:docs/self-improve/dream/*.md"
